# TalStudio

Local Gradio app for generating images (Stable Diffusion v1.5) and short music
clips (MusicGen small) from text prompts.

## Requirements

- Python 3.10+
- A CUDA GPU is strongly recommended (image/music generation will run on CPU
  but will be slow). ~8GB VRAM is a reasonable minimum since both models are
  loaded into memory at startup.

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Run

```bash
python app.py
```

Gradio will print a local URL (default `http://127.0.0.1:7860`) to open in
your browser.

## Notes

- Generated images and audio are saved under `image-generator/output/` and
  `music-generator/output/` with unique filenames, and are not committed to
  the repo (see `.gitignore`).
- The Stable Diffusion pipeline uses its default safety checker.